00:04:20,869 --> 00:04:26,869
A story of wealth, fame, power... and this guy.

2
00:08:41,739 --> 00:08:47,739
Clear History is a comedy, tv movie film directed by Greg Mottola.

3
00:13:02,608 --> 00:13:08,608
Nathan Flomm, in order to avoid the humiliation of having missed out on a hugely
successful business, assumes a new identity on Martha's Vineyard.

4
00:17:23,478 --> 00:17:29,478
He plots revenge when his former business partner moves to the same town.

5
00:21:44,347 --> 00:21:50,347
Nathan Flomm / Rolly DaVore, played by Larry David.

6
00:26:05,217 --> 00:26:11,217
Will Haney, played by Jon Hamm.

7
00:30:26,086 --> 00:30:32,086
Rhonda, played by Kate Hudson.

8
00:34:46,956 --> 00:34:52,956
Jennifer, played by Eva Mendes.

9
00:39:07,826 --> 00:39:13,826
Frank, played by Danny McBride.

10
00:43:28,695 --> 00:43:34,695
Joe Stumpo, played by Michael Keaton.

11
00:47:49,565 --> 00:47:55,565
Going Clear: Scientology and the Prison of Belief is a
2015 documentary film about Scientology.

12
00:52:10,434 --> 00:52:16,434
Directed by Alex Gibney and produced by HBO, it is based on Lawrence Wright's book
Going Clear: Scientology, Hollywood and the Prison of Belief (2013).

13
00:56:31,304 --> 00:56:37,304
The film premiered at the 2015 Sundance Film Festival in Park City, Utah.

14
01:00:52,173 --> 01:00:58,173
It received widespread praise from critics and was nominated for seven
Emmy Awards, winning three, including Best Documentary.

15
01:05:13,043 --> 01:05:19,043
It also received a 2015 Peabody Award and won the award for Best
Documentary Screenplay from the Writers Guild of America.

16
01:09:33,913 --> 01:09:39,913
The film deconstructs Scientology's claims by presenting a
condensed history of the group and its founder, L.

17
01:13:54,782 --> 01:14:00,782
Ron Hubbard, examining how celebrities interact with Scientology, and highlighting the stories of a number
of ex-members and of the abuse and exploitation that they described seeing and experiencing.

18
01:18:15,652 --> 01:18:21,652
The Church of Scientology responded vehemently to the film, complaining to film critics
about their reviews and denouncing the filmmakers and their interviewees.

19
01:22:36,521 --> 01:22:42,521
Going Clear was released in a limited number of theaters on
March 13, 2015, and aired on HBO on March 29, 2015.

20
01:26:57,391 --> 01:27:03,391
It was a major ratings success and by mid-April 2015 had attracted 5.5 million viewers,
making it the second most-watched HBO documentary in the past decade.

21
01:31:18,260 --> 01:31:24,260
It was subsequently released internationally, showing in theaters and on television
despite a sustained campaign by the Church of Scientology to block its release.

22
01:35:39,130 --> 01:35:45,130
The tone is lighthearted.
